{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Homotopy.HomotopyGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom_const","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L174-L180","doc":"The homomorphism induced by a constant map is trivial. The group-theoretic\nform of `homotopyGroupMap_const`, which is what a statement about kernels\nconsumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L170-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupHom","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L153-L168","doc":"**The induced map is a group homomorphism** (for `N` nonempty, which is\nMathlib's hypothesis for `π_N` being a group at all). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.one_eq_const_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.one_eq_const_mk","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L147-L151","doc":"The unit is the class of the constant cube — Mathlib's `HomotopyGroup.one_def`\nrestated as a `simp` lemma in the direction rewriting wants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_transAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_transAt","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L130-L143","doc":"Post-composition commutes with `GenLoop.transAt`.\n\n`transAt` is built as a `GenLoop.copy` of `fromLoop (toLoop a ⬝ toLoop b)`\nwhose *stated* underlying function is the explicit reparametrised\n`if ↑(t i) ≤ 1/2 then a … else b …`. So the claim is\n`f (if P then u else v) = if P then f u else f v`, i.e. `apply_ite` — no\npath-algebra reasoning is needed at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_const","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L113-L124","doc":"A constant map kills every class. The induced map factors through\n`π_N(point)`, which is trivial — but no such factorisation is needed: the\npushforward of any cube along a constant map *is* the constant cube, on the\nnose.\n\nThis is the easy half of exactness at the middle spot of the fibration\nsequence. `p ∘ ι` is constant on the fibre for the reason the fibre exists,\nso `p_* ∘ ι_* = 1` with no lifting property in sight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_comp","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L103-L111","doc":"Functoriality, second half: a composite induces the composite. Stated with\nthe two basepoint equations separate rather than derived, so it can be used\nin either direction without rewriting under a proof term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_id","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L96-L101","doc":"Functoriality, first half: the identity induces the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap_mk","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L92-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.homotopyGroupMap","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L87-L90","doc":"**The induced map on homotopy groups**, `π_N(X, x) → π_N(Y, y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_homotopic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_homotopic","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L78-L85","doc":"Post-composition respects homotopy rel the boundary — so it descends to\nhomotopy classes. This is `ContinuousMap.HomotopicRel.comp_continuousMap`\nwith no adaptation, because `GenLoop.Homotopic` unfolds to `HomotopicRel`\nrelative to `Cube.boundary N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L74-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap_coe","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L70-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor.genLoopMap","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/HomotopyGroupFunctor.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**Pushing a based cube forward.** If `f x = y`, post-composition with `f`\ncarries `Ω^N x` into `Ω^N y`: the composite is continuous, and on\n`Cube.boundary N` it takes the value `f x = y`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}